Package: BlockR
Title: Drag-and-Drop Clinical Trial Analysis Built on 'teal'
Version: 0.1.3
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tulio", "Author", email = "tulio@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("The Inter Project Authors", role = "cph",
           comment = "Inter font (SIL Open Font License 1.1)"),
    person("The JetBrains Mono Project Authors", role = "cph",
           comment = "JetBrains Mono font (SIL Open Font License 1.1)")
    )
Description: 'BlockR' puts a drag-and-drop canvas on top of 'teal' so that
    people who do not write R can query clinical trial data in CDISC ADaM
    format and build tables, listings and graphs. Any output of the 'TLG
    Catalog' is a starting point: its R code becomes blocks (datasets,
    filters, derived columns, table layout, statistics, plot layers),
    stacked into pipelines and wired together; every block can be edited,
    bypassed, moved, removed or added from a palette, each block shows what
    it produces (rows, a table, a plot), and the result is recomputed as
    you go. "Show R code" gives the complete, runnable code of the canvas.
    A 'TLG Catalog' page reproduces every table, listing and graph of the
    catalog on the filtered data, and the exploratory and safety
    'teal.gallery' templates remain available. A cached data pipeline
    (ingestion, pre-processing, caching) reads the synthetic datasets
    bundled with 'random.cdisc.data', freshly generated synthetic data, or
    ADaM parquet files, checked against a data contract.
